### Introduction

I am Anup Neupane and I work in the Linux OS Engineering focusing on building and standardizing RHEL platforms at scale. I design automated, secure, and consistent system builds using Ansible, manage patching lifecycle with Red Hat Satellite, and develop automation and reporting solutions to reduce manual work. Some of the projects I've been working is automating RHEL in-place upgrades, automating remediations for vulnerabilities, maintaining our server build code, rewriting custom packages, providing automation for other teams to use with documentation.

### My daily work like:

On a daily basis, my work is focused on maintaining and improving the Linux platform at scale rather than handling individual server issues. I spend a significant amount of time developing and maintaining automation using Ansible and Bash. This includes building reusable playbooks, enhancing scripts for compliance and system configuration, and creating workflows that reduce manual intervention. A big focus is making everything repeatable and reliable at scale.

## Brief intro you can use

“Thanks for meeting with us today. I’m going to ask a few Linux engineering questions. Some are scenario-based, so I’m not looking for one perfect command. I’m more interested in how you think through platform standards, automation, troubleshooting, risk, and repeatable engineering solutions.”

