# 3. RHEL 8/9 troubleshooting after patching

## Main question

“A RHEL 9 server was patched last night. After reboot, the application team says the app is down. The server is reachable by SSH. Walk me through how you would troubleshoot.”

## Clarifying bullets you can give if they need help

“You can start from the OS side. Assume you do not know yet whether it is an OS issue, application issue, network issue, storage issue, or patch issue.”

Things they can check:

- Server health
- Failed services
- Logs
- Network ports
- Firewall/SELinux
- Mount points
- Package/kernel changes
- Application logs
- Whether issue affects one server or many

## Follow-up questions

- “What commands would you run first?”
- “How would you check whether the issue is related to the new kernel?”
- “How would you check if SELinux is blocking something?”
- “How would you confirm whether the app is listening on the expected port?”
- “When would you rollback or boot into the previous kernel?”
- “How would you communicate with the app team during the issue?”

## What you are listening for

Strong answer should be organized and calm. They should not immediately reboot or rollback. They should isolate the issue: system health, service status, logs, ports, firewall, SELinux, mounts, package changes, kernel changes, and scope.

## Red flag follow-up

If they jump straight to rollback, ask:

“What would you check before deciding rollback is the right action?”

